<title>FRANCE: BoF's Trichet sticks to G7 consensus on dollar.</title>
<headline>BoF's Trichet sticks to G7 consensus on dollar.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of France head Jean-Claude Trichet said on Thursday he stuck by the Group of Seven consensus that previous exchange rate imbalances versus the dollar unit had be corrected.</p>
<p>&quot;For the moment we have a consensus in the G7...which says that the dollar has now corrected previous imbalances...I stick by this consensus,&quot; Trichet, governor of the independent French central bank, told RTL radio when asked to comment on the dollar's recent rise.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
